  "invariants": [
    "Lens is a projection of the canvas frames; every L1 node is the canonical shape on the canvas (canvasElement), never a second copy.",
    "External systems (CDN, push provider) and the client apps may reappear in the L1 frame as boundary context; they keep their L0 key and kind.",
    "No L1 service drills anywhere: the source gives no internals for the gateway, auth, upload, feed or the workers.",
    "L3 Flow, L4 Operation and L5 Source have no nodes; they are unavailable because the source is HLD only, not because a step was skipped.",
    "No node carries code evidence with a path or line range; code evidence is 'unavailable' wherever it is listed.",
    "Edges keep direction: publishers and subscribers both point at the message queue; nothing points from the queue to a service."
  ],
